  <data name="MapFlipInfo" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Map Flip function works by first adjusting the end of the video for part 1. Then, in the adjustment window, you can set the start time for the video of part 2, so it follows immediately after the end of part 1. 
It is essential that you have the complete video for the entire course and have created a set of Quickroute files (both XML and image) for each part.
You can trim the GPS track in the Quickroute files within Quickroute so that they only contain GPS data for part 1 and part 2, respectively. 
Remember to generate separate output video files for map 1 and map 2 (Make Video button). 
You can switch between map 1 and 2. Map 1 is the default map, if map 2 is active the Map Flip box will be green. The output file for Map 2 will start at the map flip start time.</value>
